{
  // Template: copy as "appsettings.Local.json" next to Duopilo.exe (e.g. C:\Tools\Duopilo\)
  // and fill in. The real file is never checked in (.gitignore) and update.cmd doesn't overwrite it.
  // Until 0.9.x the section was called "Kopilot" – an old file keeps working, saving in the dashboard renames it.
  //
  // Language:        "en" (default) or "de" – language of the dashboard, tool messages and tray. Callouts, checklists,
  //                  FMA calls, warnings, radio and logs always stay English. Also in the dashboard under Settings → Language.
  // BearerToken:     create with "Duopilo.exe --generate-secret" (at least 32 characters)
  // ConsentPassword: your own password for the consent page when connecting in Claude (at least 12 characters)
  //
  // Empty values mean: this way of access is off.
  //
  // Most of this can also be set in the dashboard under "Settings" (http://127.0.0.1:5155): access for Claude,
  // SimBrief, microphone, modules, language. The page writes to this file and keeps the comments.
  // Reports: "report a problem" in the dashboard – GitHubRepository (default duopilo/duopiloapp, empty = save locally only).
  //
  // SimBrief: Username OR PilotId (simbrief.com → Account Settings) – for get_flight_plan, get_progress and L/C/R of the ATC runway.
  // Monitoring.DisabledRules: turn rules off, e.g. [ "SPEED_DEVIATION", "ALT_1000_TO_GO", "TRAFFIC_PROXIMITY" ].
  // Monitoring.Traffic: limits of the traffic warning (ProximityRangeNm, ProximityAltitudeFt, ProximityCooldownSec, ScanIntervalSec).
  //                    AltitudeReference: "Pressure" (default, altitude difference against own pressure altitude) or "True" (against true altitude).
  //                    MessageLog: false turns off logs\traffic-messages.csv (check of the SimConnect responses, crash analysis 0.9).
  // Monitoring.FuelCheck: fuel check in cruise (IntervalMinutes, DeviationIncreaseKg, LandingBufferKg, MinSpacingMinutes) – see README.
  // Speech output (voice, output device, volume): in the dashboard under Callouts → Voice, saved in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Duopilo\speech.json.
  // Voice loop (microphone → copilot/ATC): NOT here, but in the dashboard (Callouts → Voice) or in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Duopilo\voice-settings.json.
  // Detailed log of the voice loop: "Logging": { "LogLevel": { "Duopilo.Voice": "Debug" } } (at the top level, next to "Duopilo").
  // Atc.SessionFile: backup of the ATC session (default atc-session.json in the data folder, empty = off). RestartAfterCrash: Windows restarts Duopilo after a crash.
  // Input module: locked by default. Unlock in the dashboard ("Input locked" → click twice) or here with "Input": { "Enabled": true }.
  // FirstOfficer: name and voice per flight with the voice loop (Name empty = random, Gender auto/female/male for your own name,
  //               Introduce: introduction at the briefing). Also in the dashboard under Settings → First officer and small talk.
  // Smalltalk:    optional chat with a language model, off by default. Provider "claude" (ApiKey required, Model empty =
  //               claude-haiku-5-5), "openai" (OpenAI-compatible: Url = base URL, default https://api.openai.com/v1, Model required)
  //               or "ollama" (Url of the other computer, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:11434, Model required).
  //               The ApiKey belongs ONLY here (or in the environment variable Duopilo__Smalltalk__ApiKey) – never in logs or reports.
  //               MaxReplyWords (10–150), RequestsPerMinute (1–30), TimeoutSec (2–30), UnaddressedMaxWords (0 = only when addressed by name).
  //               German voice: Supertonic (default true – Supertonic 3, ~400 MB on first use, model license OpenRAIL-M; false = Piper only),
  //               SupertonicThreads (1–16, default 2). Piper stays the fallback if Supertonic can't be loaded.
  "Duopilo": {
    "Transport": "http",
    "Language": "en",
    "SimBrief": {
      "Username": "",
      "PilotId": ""
    },
    "Monitoring": {
      "DisabledRules": []
    },
    "Remote": {
      "PublicUrl": "https://duopilo.example.com",
      "BearerToken": "",
      "ConsentPassword": ""
    }
  }
}
